cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "BioSeqInsight: an integrated desktop platform for DNA sequence analysis and validated protein structure-resource retrieval"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using these metadata, and cite the structural resources it queries separately."
type: software
version: "2.0.2"
date-released: "2026-09-23"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/niloy-999/BioSeqInsight"
url: "https://github.com/niloy-999/BioSeqInsight"
abstract: >-
  BioSeqInsight is a cross-platform desktop application and command-line tool
  that combines nucleotide and protein sequence analysis with retrieval of
  protein structures from RCSB PDB, the AlphaFold Protein Structure Database
  and the ESM Atlas fold service. Its distinguishing feature is automatic
  validation of sequence-to-structure mapping: every retrieved structure is
  aligned against the query sequence and cross-checked against its database
  accession, and the outcome is reported on an explicit five-level scale
  (M0-M4) so that a homologue or an unrelated molecule is never presented as
  the queried protein. The software has no required third-party dependencies,
  ships a 432-test offline suite, and stores the inputs, settings and software
  version of each analysis so that runs can be reproduced and shared.
keywords:
  - bioinformatics
  - sequence analysis
  - protein structure
  - structure validation
  - AlphaFold
  - ESMFold
  - RCSB PDB
  - UniProt
  - reproducibility
  - desktop application
